  <prompt>Build the config-driven record template shell for the external SPA: a `RecordTemplateConfig` per record type (title, header facts, optional tabs, left/right sections, toolbar actions) and a modal on SprkModal `lg` that renders only from that config, keeps R3's states and navigation guard, and keeps `?record={type}:{id}` deep links working. Section renderers and the switch-over come in task 005.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in React, Fluent UI v9 and the SprkModal system (ADR-050). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/` holds the config types, the six-type config map, the record reads moved out of `RecordDetailModal.tsx`, and `RecordTemplateModal.tsx`; vitest tests prove every state, the fixed chrome, the column layout classes, Refresh, Copy link and deep-link coverage; the R3 modal still works unchanged for users (it now imports the moved reads).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-01 (the per-type table), FR-02; design §3; owner 2026-11-08: title = type + number, tabs off by default, all six types. R3's `RecordDetailModal.tsx` stacks sections; its states (loading, denied, notfound, error with retry, deleted) and its `nav.onBeforeNavigate` hold (:600-628) are the behaviour to keep. The prototype `c:\code_files\spaarke-prototype\projects\2026-10-spa-record-modal\src\template\` (`types.ts`, `RecordModal.tsx`, `RecordModalHeader.tsx`, `RecordSection.tsx`) is the visual reference, not the spec.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/recordTemplate.types.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/recordTemplates.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/recordReads.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/RecordTemplateModal.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/external-spa/tests/RecordTemplateModal.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/RecordDetailModal.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/record-targets.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/RecordDetailFields.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/RecordOpener.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/RecordDeepLink.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/tests/RecordDetailModal.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkModal/SprkModal.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkModal/SprkModal.types.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/RecordHeader/RecordHeaderShell.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/theme/scrollbar.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">`RecordCommandBar` and `RECORD_ACTION_ICONS` from `@spaarke/ui-components`</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-050 / FR-02">`RecordTemplateModal` is a `SprkModal` with `size="lg"`; no bespoke envelope, no nested `RecordNavigationModalShell`. Browse uses `nav` with `onBeforeNavigate`; the footer is Close only (in `footer`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-01">The modal renders only from `RecordTemplateConfig`: no `cfg.entity === '…'` branches in `RecordTemplateModal.tsx`. A config entry gives `entity`, `label`, `titleNumberAttribute`, `headerFacts`, optional `tabs` (absent by default), `left` and `right` section ids, and `toolbar` action ids drawn from `RECORD_ACTION_ICONS` keys. The six entries match the spec FR-01 table exactly (Document has no right column).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-02">Toolbar, header and tabs stay outside the scroll area; only the content region scrolls, styled with `thinScrollbarStyle`. Left/right columns are 66% / 34% and stack (left first) when the viewport is below 1000px. Title = type label + record number (fallback: name, then label alone).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-02">States kept, each with R3's text and test id semantics: loading, denied (no field or section rendered), notfound, error (retry only when retryable), deleted; navigation held while a child operation is in flight (`onBeforeNavigate` returns false and Close is held).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-04 / FR-05">The toolbar is `RecordCommandBar`; icons come only from `RECORD_ACTION_ICONS`. This task wires Refresh (re-reads the record) and Copy link (copies `{origin}{path}?record={token}:{id}`, the inverse of `parseRecordLink`, built in `record-targets.ts`); every other action id is passed with `visible: false` until tasks 005/006 wire it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`recordReads.ts` receives `buildFetchXml`, `postFetch`, `useRecord` and `useRelatedRows` MOVED from `RecordDetailModal.tsx` (:96-227) unchanged; `RecordDetailModal.tsx` imports them. No new server read and no change to what is fetched.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens via `makeStyles` only; light, dark, high-contrast and Teams themes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not switch `RecordOpener` to the template and do not delete R3 code in this task (task 005 does both).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/spec.md</file>
