      <pattern name="Prototype template layout" location="c:\code_files\spaarke-prototype\projects\2026-10-spa-record-modal\src\template\RecordModal.tsx">Toolbar/header/columns arrangement to mirror visually.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Move the record reads into `recordReads.ts`; point `RecordDetailModal.tsx` at them; run the existing `tests/RecordDetailModal.test.tsx` to prove no change.</step>
    <step order="2">Write `recordTemplate.types.ts` and `recordTemplates.ts` (six entries per FR-01; header facts from the existing `RECORD_DETAIL_ENTITIES` fields).</step>
    <step order="3">Add `recordLinkFor(entityName, id)` to `record-targets.ts` (inverse of `RECORD_LINK_TOKENS`).</step>
    <step order="4">Write `RecordTemplateModal.tsx`: SprkModal lg, fixed chrome (RecordCommandBar, header with an empty "Your access" slot for task 006, optional TabList), scrolling content with two column regions rendering section placeholders by id through a `renderSection(id)` prop.</step>
    <step order="5">Choose the header: reuse `RecordHeaderShell` if it renders "title + up to three facts + one access line" without changing it; otherwise build it from Fluent primitives in the SPA. Record the choice in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="6">Write `tests/RecordTemplateModal.test.tsx` (vitest).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint` and `npm test` in `src/client/external-spa`.</step>
    <step order="8">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations and decisions in `projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-003-notes.md`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If fixed chrome with a scrolling content region cannot be built inside SprkModal's body without changing SprkModal, STOP and escalate (shared component, ADR-050) rather than forking an envelope.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a field in the FR-01 table has no data source today (for example a header fact not in `RECORD_DETAIL_ENTITIES` or the allow-list), leave it out, note it, and do not add a column — FR-18 (task 031) owns new columns.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`RECORD_DETAIL_ENTITIES` (`RecordDetailFields.tsx:73`) already configures fields, `documentsRoot`, `invoicesBy` and `showsEventsAndTasks` per type; `RecordDetailModal.tsx:558` renders them stacked.</existing>
    <extension>Partly: the template config reuses `RECORD_DETAIL_ENTITIES`'s field lists and the moved reads, but the stacked modal cannot express columns, tabs, toolbar actions or per-type section order, and FR-01 retires it.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-01/FR-02 fail: no type can show the two-column layout, fixed toolbar or record actions, and every later P1 task (005, 004, 006, 007) has no shell to plug into.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="States render">
      <url>{spa-dev-url}/?record=matter:{matter-id}</url>
      <steps><step>Open an accessible matter, an inaccessible one, and a missing id.</step><step>Force a failed read (offline) and press Try again.</step><step>Check the console.</step></steps>
      <expected>Loading, ready, denied, notfound and retryable error each render with R3's text; no console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Layout at three widths">
      <steps><step>Open a project at 1440px, 1000px and 375px viewport widths.</step><step>Scroll the content.</step></steps>
      <expected>Two columns (66/34) at 1440 and 1000; stacked at 375 with no horizontal page scroll; toolbar, header and tabs stay fixed while content scrolls with the thin scrollbar.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode and Teams theme (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Switch the SPA to dark, then open it in the Teams host (dark and high contrast).</step><step>Verify backgrounds, text and icons adapt.</step></steps>
      <expected>All colours use Fluent v9 semantic tokens; no white panels in dark mode.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">typecheck, lint and vitest in src/client/external-spa</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/recordTemplate.types.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/recordTemplates.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/recordReads.ts</output>
